One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
For with the time her babe should run,
And from her goes all her store;
As, to prevent hap, she goes about
Making old women's hours and old men's wrinkles new.
She stores all her wealth in fairings,
And all her skillfulness in looks informs.
And having all these, she subjects her pleasure
To different hours and things;
And spends all her wealth in shows,
Which she confounds to perfection.
  All her good is merchandized whose rich delight
  Toasts every vulgar delight.


