When my heart in my body moans and groans,
To weep in my soul's vitals,
Like to death, in a kind of transgression?
O, no, I have no such passion, love,
As you in my body canst from me speak;
And therefore are you my friends only in my bosoms.
Ah, but in my moans and groans,
When in yours I almost cry out,
And in mine own loving words state that I do so:
  "Hath no such hatred in you from me."


