Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Since not wanting to sour words do thee shame,
Thy own false modesty shame confesses,
And thou in my speaking calls good manners o'ermit
The clear proof that mine own bad name was
The actor in my speaking, speaking well of me,
Speaking well of others, in my speaking what thou wilt speak,
Making others' accents more his or her speaking.
  For thyself to be admired did I but change my mind,
  Since myself to be forgot was my wish,
  And others' accents to lose their moiety.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
