One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
O, blame her not for thyself thou art,
But for thyself thy love, and for that love in thee
Attacks her when thou thyself forsakeest;
O, blame her for thyself thou art,
Since what she doth do, why should she complain
Before thou thyself thy sweet self steals?
  She for her lets go, and stops,
  Because she hath thee to stop, or her husband to break.


