Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Stirred by dark to their white.
For why, then, poor souls in hue,
Who look upon thy beauty and thy fair face,
Whilst I, drawn even by thy loving thoughts,
Gain access to thy sweet niggard parts,
Have idle patience, all naked,
For thy fair appearance alone doth make my heart mad
And every unfair dealing boy to me doth steal thy treasure.
  Let this sad int'rim like the ocean be
