Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Thy looks with black eyes no whit are painted.
For there can live no hatred in thy complexion;
Thy looks with thy complexion's shade leave out,
Die to themselves, and in them thine eyes are hid.
For thy looks in mine are true, and therefore my soul
Is raven black, and there dwells no love in thine eyes.
  But if thy thoughts be true and thou gav'st me rest,
  My body then with thy thoughts must be sold.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
For then my grief's not enough to drown me,
It must be gentle enough to weep for my friend,
And I will bear it even to the edge of doom.
O, if, though my friend be cast away,
The grief that I feel then must leave,
My lover, by all means welcome returned,
As my body's rich ransom cannot be untaken.
  But if my friend be poisoned,
  The loss is not so great, but I must be buried,
  And my love must live on despite that.


