Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Looking for my body where thou art, to cry "Bless me thou hast slain."
Since thou, thyself so cruel hath sold
The wondrous beauty and the rarest of all-purchased commodities,
And for thy sweet sport bred thine own fair,
But my love that needs no defense doth blunt,
Stealing thy treasure away, for mine is thee.
