O, that my worst moan may exceed your blest
Thy inward pride's equal; so thy outward praised boast
Shifts place with equal twain, and all alike on high.
Therefore thy worst moan, far greater than mine,
Come to my aid, do me injury; send me th' inferior wretch to plead
My cause before this captain's shop;
Thou, whom thou thyself hast heavily greeed,
Sets me cross-referencing thee for an acquaintance.
  This quest alone shall make me woe, but I will bear it.


