One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
Her husband, on the other hand, is more fond
On the virtuous behavior of his wife's
And lays a dearer burden on his widow's breast.
In his drooping respects their chief delight
Is found in their consummated groan,
And, rank not by rank but by rank ranks placed,
Sets down his widow on to task,
Strikes, hits and kills, all his wealth away.
  To win she must bear his cruelty,
  As then proceeds a virtuous life.


