And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may live.
Thence comes it that I list all mine means;
And what of thee thyself thy sweet love doth give
Hath mine own spoil of thy sweet self buried.
So then, of thyself I may not boast;
Yet that, for thyself I must allege,
When thou art all ruined, all me for thee.
  In sum my grave lies but a short distance from thee;
  But since thee and me and thee alone,
  Then let that space for thyself calculate
  When other men's gardens yield thee small soil.


