By shifting the pace of her swift work,
And her born-up counterpart declines
To entertain the wakened muse with her cries.
Possessing or pursuing, thou hast her all;
Yet in these last words doth she plead:
  Me thou hast her all, and I have her all,
  In seeming simplicity and truth come next.


