Even the fairest of days volunteering her for thee?
Proving a worthier breed by succession thine,
So thou hast her thrice more than her poor consort,
And she in more delight doth find
Than from thee thine own sweet thief.
  Make her wert thou when thou art gone, though she still live;
  Or if thou live remembered not to be,
  Give her thyself back again after many a bad fight.


