It might with some weed take hold of the weed,
But that weed dead must die, and must in his transgression be mourned;
For sweetest love, when it is won,
Shall weeds play dead and decay as fast as weeds grow;
But, being won, the win takes away all hope.
  Hence, no love toward others,
  No love toward anybody's death.


O me, what eyes hath love put in my head,
