And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine is not free.
He can have no other than a common grave,
And no private widow well may keep,
By children's eyes, her husband's shape in mind.
But since he died and poets better prove,
I have found such a mansion in her cheek
As the old world as thou art,
And given thee such a mansion yield
Than of thyself to me,
Which used lives thine and born of thee.
  There lives more life in one of her fair eyes
  Than both her poets can in praise devise.


