And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
Since all alike my soul and all my every part,
Is one, of one, still pleasing note do hang
Upon that star's celestial face,
Whose worth's unknown, although his height be taken.
Thence comes it that my soul's imaginary sight
