And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may lie.
Now I'll give thee back what thou ow'st, and I'll give
As much as I can to my needy self,
So that thou in my debt mayst live
And do what thou wilt with me.
This thou gav'st, to thyself thou gav'st,
And I to myself will part;
To myself thou gav'st but what thou ow'st,
And I to myself will part;
So that all our arising may be one,
And one of us shall die.
  Then other me thou gav'st,


