One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
In the process of nature's fury she confounds
And hugely exaggerates her own beauty;
In sequent toil she stores,
And nothing stands but for her to mow.
So, like a miser on the edge of the woe,
I'llil without caring whether her fleece be
Or whether she live or die.
  She wastes no time in her errors,
  Being a mother of monsters and quick to anger.


