Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the brood-home where she breeds.
The canker that ate her fled,
And as for her to breed another,
The same fell prey to the canker,
And, like her, died young; but, like her,
A third time her beauty stole,
And, like her, died a second youth.
Then, if she had lived alone,
Her beauty remembered no beauty,
But, like her, died a third time.
  In her beauty's fight were sweetest things slain,
  And men much vied with one another to see 't.


