And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may have life.
So shall my life be spent in honor
And love's treasure be hid in ignorance
--wherein thou dost lie, almost assured
Of my theft--in the recesses of thy brain.
In other words, I can live no longer in this flattery;
Therefore to give up myself thou hast the strength
To suffer my life when I am strong enough to die.
  So thou keep'st me so for love of him that I will never give
  Up that which thou ow'st.


