That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Who for beauty's sake lies to me scorn;
For such a lie hath my heart in love sunk,
And, like a stone in a pond,
My love's history repeats itself thrice.
I do believe, though I not think so,
That love hath a story to tell.
  For there can live no hatred in love's brow,
  Unless that pencil which truth doth ink draw.


