Thou that art thy self so great mayst prove;
For thou thyself murd'rous murd'rous murd'rous wert born,
And like a lamb doth chide the world,
Who for thy great deed doth mock his looks,
Thy self so great murd'rous murd'rous wert born.
  But I swear by my love that I will not deny thee this;
  For thou, thy self so great, wert so vile born.


