For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And, in them, the worth of love lies.
Thou art beloved of many, of many a few,
And yet I will not change my mind
That thou in me stands still, as the statue stands,
Looking on things as they are,
That thinking on things that are not
Cannot in me conversion stop,
  Unless my heart were altered in some willful
  Way.


