Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And that beauty which on thy cheek doth live
With my love's color is counterfeit.
Thou art thy own state, and that beauty doth lie,
Made more by thy state than by my love's substance;
For thou art the more excellent part of me,
Since by thy sweet state I am nothing.
  In that I am thee, in love thou art my all,
  And I, in nothing.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
