One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
But since each leaves his shop,
One thing is left to do, and that is to care
For his dear domesticated nurse.
So each puts his shop, his dress, his food,
And in the frame of his mind
Plods carefree in his wonted joy.
  But what of his care is left,
  Save that in his breast doth live his love,
  That keeps him from theft or death.


