Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may inherit.
He is so fair in so ill plight
That he shall in thy power thrive
And I in him be nothing, captive to his will;
So I will leave him and take what is best.
He will live, though I be wracked in hell,
For thou dost devise such a deal
As mine own desert cannot be exchanged,
For it is thy love that keeps mine eye awake.
  But if my love be bas'ring in thy brain,
  The basest of criminals shall live!


