They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And that is this, that they which find it
In thy brain, thy sweet self, convert it to mine.
For nothing stands so well for a jewel to lay,
Nor hath beauty ever so fair been borne,
Whereto men of sense chose it as their object.
So then thou fool, and most false, in pursuing
