One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
But when the raven that calls on her favor
Appears, lo, she no sooner calls,
But hast the babe in her breast devour,
Stealing away the profit of her keep.
So she debateth with loss and gain,
Gain by and by and by again debateth,
Until, all in war with loss and gain,
The same disgrace, this time from one,
Sets thee again on thy way.
  Such is the pattern of folly,
  That, each changing place, in his pride lies.


