Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
To look on thy fair morn
While my heart hath that mournful itch again.
So, being made of one, I must each day stay
One, both heart and eyes in one,
Looking on thee with divided minds,
Resembling sire and child and friend
Who, all in one, one sad plight hold;
One, from thy loving parts, to thee I send;
Another, to thee from me doth send this message:
