Another hath his pleasure removed,
And that too with me; yet another hath died,
And that grief in me still grieves.
Thou art as fair in my view,
As I in my other's, though not so bright,
For that my saucy tint doth change colour;
And, for thy sake, in my thoughts also doth change.
