And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may have life
And benefit of thy sweet will.
Then, if for my life thou wilt permit,
I can give thee what I want; but if not,
Then thou wilt forfeit me both thine and I die.
He can have no love from me but in so fair
As mine own true worth gives;
And yet, by so fair a creature agreeing,
He gains both by mine own desert and I die.
  But if he love not mine own true worth,
  Then thou too mine, and I too die.


