What can be so sacred but thy love?
What's so dear that thou dost promise so high,
And so seldom achieve?
Come, let us divided live
And then I will confess that he is thee,
And my love for him then be determined,
By my loving-kindness then existing,
Against his granting another thee this right.
  So thou divide'st thyself, and I am thee,
  That we two may live in perfect love,
  Or, if our parts should fail, by halves to blame.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
