Of my love's being deceived,
That I might not know her to be deceived there.
I take great pleasure in seeming false to her,
That she may think no ill of what I think,
And yet by my seeming falsehood bring
To perfection what in imperfection already lies.
  For whether beauty, birth, or wealth, or wit,
