Now, wherefore should a woman's jealousy lead,
When not even her husband's eye
Can keep pace with the jade of heaven?
O, blame not her pride, for she knew
What a joy to be had by running after him,
A prize so dear that no woman could hope to keep.
She loved him dearly indeed, but that love was not her measure;
  To her it was a duty to keep his pride.


