One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of that which flies with her.
Pity the nimble thief, and like a gazelle
Steals her way, like a swain gone mad,
For she hath no name, no dear beloved held,
But is all accounted a lark of delight.
Then, if she survive, much glory befalleth;
But if not, much dishonor befalls.
  Pity her, and she will be your treasure,
  Save as she stole your dear love.


