In pursuing her prey, her beauty so follows,
That her drooping leaves seem to hang still,
Stealing away her treasure, which is so dear
To her dear love, as fast as she can pay it;
  And, for fear of being outwitted,
  All alone she robs and lives, becoming a swindler.


