One on another's neck, to acknowledge
Thy self thou art wont to be;
And, to each other's addictions,
One on another's nerves, to acknowledge
Thy self thou art wont to be.
Such is the fair that thou art wont to be,
And yet I know it to be false,
A false friend in love's cheek,
That thou art both my foe and my friend;
  For thou art so fond on my addictions,
  That, for thy sake, I must grind my teeth.


