Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Attending on my obsequious steps;
Yet my verse, being fond on praise,
Hath thisiment: "Thou art beloved of mine eyes,
And for that love dost lie,
As subject to be politicized
And abused in thy shop."
And, to be sure that is not false,
Aunt Flo's eyes are my eyes, and they love me even
When thou, in them, art expressing
Thy true spirit and thy good will.
  But why then do I love them so?
  To know thy heart is to love me truth proves.


