For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
To hear my wretched song whilst I praise thee?
Even so my friend should suffer for my crime,
And I, to hear him complain seem dumb,
Speaking of thy worth and faults to none but thee.
O, that I could drown such a sorrow in rhyme,
And that my lover's woe might be expressed
More richly in a love song than in my verse!
  But be thou; I cannot write of thy worth,
  Unless thou take that right from me.


