And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine may have title
To that which I before had.
But what shall be the gain of this crime?
The world cannot be so cruel as mine appetite,
Nor yet my self so unprovident,
Although my will be enforced to such a pitch
As 'gainst my extreme sensibility.
O, what a mansion have I found,
Where beauty and wealth dwell together,
Where all have access to all, even to me!
  Yet this happy me thou hastst not found,
  Because thou art so possessed with murd'rous hate.


