One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the place where the foul monster grew.
So the husbandry of love, though it last night be
As night and day before,
Or both and each in twain,
So long as love lived or died,
The universe in harmony would do his will,
And make of one sweet husband some mother
That bears his cross as he walks.
  But lo, this wondrous chance affords
  The universe no such pity.  He that bears his cross, or walks,
  Makes one sweet husband after his fashion.


