But do not so. I love thee in such sort
As, thou being mine, mine is thy good report;
So shalt thy love be taken from me,
And my bad report deemed untrue.
Thou that art so fond on form should change
Within my breast, from mine eye;
But that thou mayst change not thy mind,
Feed'st thy old love with new intelligence.
  This change is effected by thy love;
  If I cease to love thee, thou no sooner hat'st me,
  But I give myself authority to change my mind.


