Without my consent, not subject to my will,
Although mine eye bears it in love's eye.
  This is my chamber where thoughts of love dwell,
  Where time and outward form do define.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To find another, to keep pace with her.
So I, a husband and father, do away
With time's injurious hand, and keep pace with the time;
Nor think the universe with my absence watch,
Nor think the eternal while it moans
At the base of my weary brow,
But, like a sad slave, sufferance me,
And patience tell of woes to come.
  Pity me, then, and wish I were renewed,
  For as long as thou wilt live, so long still I live!


