As, lo, myself for my part devouring,
Bearing the canker that grew in her,
Feed'st my love's contents to the flame,
Making a famine where abundance lies,
Culling the herd to eat the taker;
  And, possessing all, quite unthrifts me
  To scorn, to scorn I call myself content.


