Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Since my poor eyes were new and old,
And from thee this I commend,
Since thou no longer canst know my heart.
Thine eyes are windows to my heart,
Which in thy breast doth live, as thine eyes in me;
And thine lips, when they look on thee in me,
The basest jewel doth willfully appear.
