Those lips that Love's own hand did make
Breathed forth the sound that said "I hate"
To me that languished for her sake;
My tongue-tied lips to that same rage
Have put a spirit of youth in everything,
That heavy tears, bigots, and wrinkles strange.
But those same lips that I loved inher,
Inher than she wrought thee, she carved
And therein change my love to that I hold.
Thy outward thus with outward praise is crowned,
