Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;
Bring me within thine objectively,
And there reigns beauty and goodness at a tilt
Like pinpoints in the sweet'st flame.
Kindness that smothers with a show
Such fires will heat my blood to boiling pitch
And straight flames might do violence to my breast;
For there reigns more joy in one's life
Than in thine, which proves more blest
By thy sweet love.
  I believe this to be true, and yet might
