Tyranny in love is far more intolerable
Than that in itself reigning abuse,
Which strangely lends ease to suffering people.
O, that our unhappy times could be divided
Rather than that we suffered in our errors,
That sorrow might crown our rights,
And ease us of our sorrow with sweet words.
  But thou, to whom my tears are shed,
  Shall not take my sorrow from thee,
  Although mine end may prove harder.


