For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And there reigns love and all hate in twain
One crowned help, which is seldom found
Other than in thy power to fortify me.
I grant, sweet love, thou mayst annotate my will,
And perhaps to some foreign tongue provide
