Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
That she may attend to the alackpresent
The blazon of her lov'st husbandry;
So I, true of thee, keep silence,
And love's sweet face for posterity
With gentle ornament,
That thou alone in posterity
Shall know thy sweet secret child;
  From hence thy sweet face shall not be forgot,
