Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of his tattered garments;
As a dying mother takes delight
To see her babe reigned in death,
As from a tomb where life embalms,
So from this sin there is no clear boat,
Nor repairable cushion to lie on.
Sin, in short, is death to Life;
And, till Life's sweet revenge be done,
No remedy can make it right.
  Presumed on thy defects,
  Mine be a curse, and thy sweet form a misery.


