Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
Without allowing my friend to suspect any injury?
O, how much more quiet should my wooing seem
If my worthy love to you had not a cause to groan,
As our mutual acquaintance threatened with instant death!
I cannot therefore be so vile as to seek anger
And plagues of worms to please you with sport;
I cannot boast that I am so bent
Or that you with worms are so vile lodged.
  For that cause therefore that friend which I love cannot choose
  But groan and complain of you of length.


