Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of his tattered best;
So thou, poised to leap the fray,
With ease passest by the strong offense,
And, weary of triumph, the foe is bidden
To humbug thee on; to give thee time
To think up a more delicious wonder.
Now think what a wondrous aid
The prey of thy love has been;
A buried treasure cannot boast so much;
Therefore to give them from thee is full of desire.
  But then, if they be slain,
  Thou win'st but thyself; their wealth is thine.


