But brief years decrease and lessen,
And terrors much greater than I thought.
Thine eyes, that taught the dumb on high to sing
And heavy ignorance aloft to fly,
Have added feathers to the learned's wing,
And given grace a double majesty.
  But thou, that hast mine eyes, wilt prove
  Even more graced than I, being fond on thee.


