Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
For my friend and I are one;
So then he that bears my love away,
Deserves it not to me but to thee.
In so profound abysm I throw all care
Of others' voices that my moan may not be heard
Beyond the ken of this censure.
For how do I hold myself apart
From thy strong tongue, which in thy flow
Doth my innermost thoughts raise a moan?
  O, care not how thy praise may sound,
