And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine might live.
So long as men can breathe or eyes can see,
So long lives this joy; but when they slide
Into darkness and dead night,
Thy sweet love's light becomes blacker than death's black night;
And, for some unexplained reason,
The phantom of thy sightless love stays awake
While thoughts of this world do from thee proceed.
  Then, if for my sake thou art true,
