O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
What is 't but half faith, half envy,
Half love, half hate, all alchemy mixed?
How are our dear crimes so neatly lodged,
Half love, half hate, all unknown art?
Why, like widowed women mightst thou live,
Without all aid, in subject to theft,
For thee alone my love corresponds;
  For thee, my friend, my equal, my witted son,
