And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.thy soul check thee that I come so near,
Swear to thy blind soul that I was thy will,
And will, thy soul knows, is admitted there.
Against this shall I ensconce me in thy breast,
And in this way shall my love hold out:
Thy small blind love is such a strength that it may hold out
Against the wrackful siege of mine eye,
Or, being broached, must yield the prey.
So long as I am with thee, so long lives this love;
But when I go, so long lives this love away.
  To give away thy sight would be consigned
  To death, where thou art delivered from me.


Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And yet they looked on thee as if thou were
One of those fair ribbons hanging in dunghill.
That is their thought, that thou mayst obsequiously slide
Upon the rest, with their frowning brow;
And having climbed the steep-up heavenly hill,
Which steep-up growths not with thine,
Yet gives them great joy, being surcharged with thee.
  But if they see farther, farther off,
  They neigh and look on thee with sad frown,
  As if thou were some strange idol that they saw.


When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
When everything that she says is commented
On particulars; but when she says
"I love you so," I know it is for true love only,
And for that love which she implies.
O, let her words be but words of love,
And I, for my part, but speak of love;
So shall tongues, for their flourish, but write
Of scraps and comments of a dead tongue,
Who lived and died for this love of yours.
  If I read this book that sits on your knee,
  The knees that taught you to walk on the ground.


