And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May glory in thy loss and pay it thee.
For thee, against myself I'll vow debate,
And though I lose, yet I'll boast a triumph;
Even so, beauteous Giuseppe, thou prevent'st
Myself from being sole owner of myself.
If I lose, do thee wrong,
And do not forget me for one moment;
Tomorrow I'll repay thee thy loss and do thee good.
  But do not so. I love thee so,
  That, for thy right, myself will offend.


