One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of her unwitting husbandry;
So I, to whom thou art so wary,
Enable thine own sweet speech to speak
To thy hurt soul when thou savest with me.
"Thou art my best of love," I say,
"And for that love thou shouldst come;
Against myself I can set down no cause,
Nor think the injury done me for nothing.
  But yet be blamed if I do not mend;
  For nothing this wide universe I call,
  Save thou, my rose; in it thou art my all.


