Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Which strips thee of thy precious age.
In others' looks thou dost love,
And therein confirmed I read,
Thy love was never so true
As in thy own heart;
Therefore to those eyes I appeal deliver
Thyself from bonds of woe,
And implore their pity with tenderness.
  In others' looks thou dost hate,
  And there reigns love and all love's loving parts,
  And all ill a true friend to me.


