For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
Without the fear of commitment,
When in the race to death I am held back?
No, love, it is not enough that hate thrusts into my breast,
Nor my friend's pain befits his rage;
It is enough that I should weep alone,
Without all nearness to anyone's hand.
O, that our night of woe might have remembered
My true love's entreaty to thee,
And in thy bosom's deep cut would seem
No more than a dream or a dreamer's view.
  But that my love's woe should seem
