O, lest my bad temperament should lead
To slandered words of ill-will,
Do not so much as my bad complexion give
That abuse my good nature for aye.
My trouble is not tongue-tied consternation
But coerced silence; in a word,
My bad feeling is extreme ignorance.
  For why should my heart struggling
  Want words to tell of thy sorrow?


