Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And I in thee think nothing strange.
In our nature is based a holy love,
That in ourselves thou mayst call king;
That in our state we all enjoy
Guiding thy Spirit in what it woos;
That for ourselves alone thy love loses
That due of due belongs to thee.
In our state we are all one,
Though ourselves isolated out of thine,
That by thy love we all thrive and all die.
  Such is the state of love that in it thou dost lose,
  That thou alone for myself alone pays the penalty.


