They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
But not what it is made of.
For through their seeing thou get'st sight,
And they in thy soul's thought do process
Thy sweet effect as if by thy sight.
They look on the flower, but not the mind,
So thou dost give them the smell,
And they taste it, and they approve it;
More, they wish it were as this,
And that therefore thou shouldst be kind.
  For best is by evil still made better;
  So thou prefiguring have thy love made.


