Against thy unfairness have I no cause,
Unless thou take that part of me thou ow'st,
And I by thee forbear all offense.
If I obey thy call, do thee homage,
And in public speak of my sport
Such praises as thy sweetly sweet lips would sing.
  But do not so. I will complain
  That thou war'st on my sport and weaknesse.


Be wise as thou art cruel; do not press
