In jollity, I do love thee in such sort
As, thou being mine, mine is thy good report;
And for their bad I find a joy
That weighs heavily on my hate.
Thou canst not, love, take from me my treasure;
I have spent all my fee simple,
And therefore have this wealth distrained from thee.
  But thou canst my riches esteem,
  And I thence derive both my pleasure and my grief.


