Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
And there reigns love and all love's loving parts,
And all those friends which I hate in thee.
How would my love be complete
If all those images I had in mind
To form some kind of double love for thee were true!
O, but these are false images,
Made more true by thy sweet virtuous love.
They are false, but true in thy seeing,
And for this I love, and this make me woe.
  But seeing them true, I change my mind,
  And in their opinions I mar the picture.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of her familiar teeming home.
The bloody warrior famous for worth,
After a thousand victories once foiled,
Is all silvered over with small loops,
And all wound up in new livery new.
Thus have I seen the lords of my time
Resemble spring and summer's color,
Or county fair, in pleasant air,
Charleston on his way to green.
  But since they live no more to tell,
  Therof my love's sweet change is.


