Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Who themselves for their love glance on thee
And to thy blackened background cry:
"Thou art our elder brother,"
"Our elder sister,"
"Our third sister,"
"Our first mother,"
"Our first daughter,"
"Our second mother,"
"Our second daughter,"
"Our first born child,"
"Our second born child,"
"Our first born woe,"
"Our second woe,"
"Our first born love."
  All these sayings I hear,
  And all these add up to sorrow.


