Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Which shall be most my torment, being tongueless.
In thee I find the just and true sorrows
Which wounded bosoms cannot adequately console;
And in thee I read such mysteries
As truth and beauty shall together thrive
If this Truth could hang in rhyme.
