Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;
Do not leave me prisoner in the thought
Of thy just deserts, though thou steal thee my love.
O, do not, when I am laced with thy blood,
Give me thought to vex thy justice;
Admit me not to the mean wherein thou art lodged,
