For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
When thou teachest how to relieve me?
O, no, more than that; for I'll not be asked
So great a price for my debtors pardon.
Be thou the tenth love of my heart,
And I shall live thy tenth life indeed.
Then may I dare to boast how I do love thee;
Be thou the tenth part of my soul,
And I ten times happy.
