For where is my strength so dull and base
That thou mayst my silence confound
And mock my virtuous pride?
O, none, unless this miracle have might,
That in the thoughts of others' tongues
Thy sweet self may be forgot,
And other's thoughts give thee light.
So then I am not dumb, poor, nor despised
Whilst that this mockery doth such substance give
That I in other's thoughts do witness
Thy fair name, what I most enjoy,
Exceeded by others' praise.



