And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May profit by thy behavior.
For to thy sensual fault I bring in sense--
The guilty one hath fled, the just one to die.
Thy looks with me, thy heart in other place.
So then I am not at all aggrieved,
Grim nor glutton, hungry nor famished,
He who so glut theorld with his looks,
He who robs the world of his sweet grace,
To thee I send this written apology--
  To give thee that due, which thou deserv'st alone.


