One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of her hawks and hounds;
So I, made yellow by my former hue,
Run after my lover's shadow,
And give him leave to mole forth
In ugly networks of wires;
And having found him, ride him home
Like a drop of water in the canker;
He that so much loves and follows
After him will be his own self-love beguiled,
For he will no sooner leave me,
For I am necessitated to go there.
  There lives a god in love,
  And he hath his angels to do good deeds.


