Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
Since thy love hath put on chestnut hue.
In that I may not grieve, though in thought thou hast lost me,
Thou art so strongly in my purpose bred
That I in thy will feel nothing;
And even thence I know thy will, and therefore cannot seem
To feel pity or to beguile the world with us.
In so profound abysm I throw all care
