O, call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;
I will not praise that which thou dost not pay.
If thou wilt leave me, let it be said
That I did strive to mend; if thou wilt stay,
That I will strive to mend still more.
O, pity me not if thou wilt leave me,
For I cannot blame thee for my love or thee for my grief;
Nay, love, be a muse to my sensual muse.
  Give my poor eyes a restful night,
  And chide thy sweet thief when she turns her thoughts to thee.


Be wise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words expresswise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words express
Thy love or thyself in a better light.
Be thou as thy presence is, gracious and kind,
And chide thyself for thy failings not knowing
How to mend thy deeds when thou art writ in verse.
Rise, resty song; my gracious salve is thine.
If in bad humor thou wax figure
Like a makeless wife, my love may be withered,
And thy love, made tongue-tied, tell a lie.
  Pity me, then; but think not
  I cannot pity thee because thou art bad.


In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And that with their wrongthink I answer.
In other words, believe me, my love is as fair
As any mother's child, though not so bright
As those gold candles fixed in heaven's air.
But when they see thee walk, their eyes are so fixed
That I in them see things they should not;
And, love, despite their false alchemy,
Thy hot fire ever burn'st a pure thrift.
  How like Eve's apple doth thy beauty grow,
  If thy sweet virtue answer not thy show.


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
