Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of her inactive flame,
Which but today by chance meet,
Tomorrow brightened in his former light.
So I, to the tender care of my verse,
Give full vitality to that which holds steady
Against the scythe and will devour
If ever the wretch be devoured,
Tomorrow's child, though yet young,
Will bear his like as he grew before.
  To give, like him, tomorrow's son
  When he is old and basely die.


