And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May take thou captive, let him keep me locked up in his brain
And torture me with thoughts of love,
Imagine me a sovereign, enjoyin' thee
As though thou were a deity.
But confess I am not well acquainted
With such a heaven as this hath got,
Where five talents, five grants, are able
To make one thing more blessed than another.
  Make me another self for love of you,
  That beauty still may live in thine or thee.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
