That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And yet they compare it with some strange sight.
They look into the excellence of thy kidneys,
And, churls, their thoughts are disposed to wane;
Yet in their wills at times are seen
