I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
Of late educated or former owner.
But since she hath cheated me of that,
I cannot blame her for my love;
I do not think it wrong to approve
Of what she doth for love of me include.
As against a canker in the fragrant rose
Which on the soft and balmy day sings,
So I myself against myself uprear
And smother my love with a thinker's rage.
  But if I lose thee, my loss is my love's gain,
  And losing her, my friend hath found that loss.


