Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
With vacant eyes their former hue;
Yet doth this change in me happen,
That my eyes' former hue are now changed:
From thy bright eyes black shall come thy dye,
And tears shall come to my eyes' eyes,
As they do now, with yellowing grey.
