I will not rebuk thy disrespect, suspect thy wrong,
Give thee thy due as thy merit doth yield.
Give thyself thy due as thy nature doth afford,
And I will give thee my respect, humble as thy lowliness brings,
Serving thee with my hate, gentle as thy gentleness proves.
I will not praise thy skill, thy wealth, thy beauty,
