Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
While nature so aptly slams me with injuries,
That thou gav'st me this lowly place,
To look on thee and on myself as thine and mine own?
O, no. Torture cannot make me sick
Of looking on thee and on myself like thine.
I feel too much oppression to be sick of it,
And therefore to be sick of it is most painful.
  Presume not on thy pity, sweet friend;
  I am not sick of it because thou art sick.


