In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And for that love is in my thought the greatest.
That love is built up with many partitions,
Which seem to me but thinly worn rarities;
But that love is not so builded with windows,
Or curtains of steel so hung with rich tincture.
That love is an ever-changing facade,
Utt'ring old offenses and adding new fortresses;
It is the freshest reinforcement to an already strong one.
  That is my love's worth, and that is all my argument.


