Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
What good turns thou against me when mine eye doth shine?
Dost thou not wonder at my graces being diminished,
Since mine own true love is made to sullied dullness by thy crime?
No, thou art blamed; I do wonder, though dumb,
At thy virtuous accuracy being strangled,
And wonder what good it can do till I see it done.
Then, be a satire to my kindness,
