Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
Of her careless way;
So I, to whom thy robb'ry lends,
Based on thy might, write this,
That thou mayst taste of my love when thou parts
From me this short time.
Thou hast passed by the ambush of young days,
Either not assailed, or victor being charged;
Yet this thy praise cannot be so thy praise
To tie up envy, evermore enlarged.
  For thy full birth is still to be remembered,
  Even as the flower that youngly doth thrive.


