Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
As I solace in thy sweet white;
Now all is done, have what shall have no end.
Thou dost love me because thou know'st my countenance,
And for that wealth of thy glass I thank thee,
For all that grace and all that truth doth lie in it.
