Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
When other petty griefs have done their spite,
To make me tongue-tied speaking of my pain?
Ah, but my love is so strong, and so worth,
That I cannot but say fair things of it,
And give them praise where I think their worth most great.
How can I then be blamed if other mock me,
When other people's bad speak of me with my hearsay?
  No, I am not self-willed;
  I am so possessed with murd'rous love that I do offend
  Even to myself alone.


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
May not vex me with dreams of separation.
So then I am not vexed
At all times with thinking on others' wills,
Save when I myself am determined
To do aught contrary to thy desire.
Thou canst not vex me with inconstant mind,
Since that my soul and heart are one;
Therefore to thy fair praise I sing,
Even as the lark at break of day
Plods pleasantly on, still more happy than before.
  Since then I can do no wrong
  Save what I think good, always true.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
Not knowing thy will, though in my tongue
Thy sweet favor shall be construed.
O, what a slur upon my humor
Doth my poor genealogy bring,
Which unwittingly ranks me second to thy dearest
And than which I can provide no praise.
Thou dost pity my foible, and lov'st it not
More than my true love lends to thy hymns;
Therefore to thy pure and most most loving mind
I add this Concord:
  Love is better than hate to me,
  Because I love thee more.


