And thou, dumb, hath no comprehension
Of what I say; for thou art
In my thoughts, and I am thy slave,
Stirred and vexed till thou begin.
Then happy I, that love and am beloved
Whilst that this hatred I hold in thine eye,
And that thou dost teach me to hate
By means which I cannot assent;
  For that same hate which I feel for thee
  Din't know thy sweet thoughts from thy sour form.


