Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
With ugly odors and their counterfeit faces,
With sick muse and their sick muse,
With false borrowed face and false borrowed phrase;
And for a while they were kind,
They had thy hair and could give thee memory;
But now, for their art,
Thou dost foist upon thy heart
And lay great bases for eternity.
  Lo, what a torment wouldst thou prove
  When thou didst forsake me for some fault.


