For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And on thy love their own fears;
How can I then hold Time's fickle glass,
And find the brave day sunk in hideous night,
When hours have drained his blood and filled his brow
With lines and wrinkles;
Then thou through windows of thine age shalt see,
Despite of mouthed graves will give thee memory;
Then thou through windows of thine age shalt see,
Despite of wrinkles, this thy golden time.
  But if thou live remembered not to be,
