Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
I cannot blame thee for my pleasure,
Although yet be blamed if thou bear'st
The blame of mine own defect.
Even so my pleasure hath to thee
Arous dependency;
So thy great deserts, which now appear
But things removed that hidden in thee lie.
Why not now thou is blamed usurer;
Now thou stand'st a lawful plea,
And patience must be thy chief desire kept.
  Hence, like a sad slave, stay and think of nought
  But as thyself doth stay and think of nought.


